data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":303,"item_id":"fc_0069d789f0da6885016adf74d26f788191bdb8e8c6f8e3e1a6","output_index":0,"arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"version\":2,\"policy\":\"endpoint-fidelity-2\",\"source_inventory_sha256\":\"f370e67d8a684ba8ec7360da0908afff5f84ed8672df715681f02891420d73ca\",\"entries\":{\"P\":{\"selector\":\"decl:AuditBExport.P\",\"expected_type\":\"∀ (n : ℕ) (E : Set (V n)) (h_H001 : E.Nonempty) (h_H002 : IsCompact E), dimH (cyl n E) = dimH E + 1\",\"correspondence\":{\"mode\":\"direct\",\"explanation\":\"The parameters n:ℕ and E:Set(V n) are exactly all nonnegative ambient dimensions and Euclidean subsets; H001 and H002 are precisely nonemptiness and compactness. W n has the n original Euclidean coordinates and one final real coordinate, so cyl n E is E×[0,1] with the specified Euclidean metric, including n=0. The coordinate functions pack, projX and projT implement this identification directly, not a max-metric product. Native dimH is the source's extended-nonnegative supremum definition with the Borel structure; T001 identifies Hmeasure with the unnormalized native covering measure. The conclusion is the original dimension identity in ℝ≥0∞. T005 proves finiteness rather than assuming it. No second metric representation is introduced.\"}}},\"library_terms\":{}}}"}

